A||||11||88GTURBO||1/8 mile to 1/4 mile times||||1||
Z||000000||88GTURBO||12-12-2001||12:11 AM||||I have a 1/8 mile time slip and would like to know what the 1/4 mile time would be. Is there a web site that will calculate this info and give me an est. 1/4 time? <BR>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||I wish I had a GT||12-12-2001||12:19 AM||||If there is I would be greatly suprised.  There are a lot of variables that would effect the 1/4 time.  Really the best estimation of a time is to double your 1/8 mile.  <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>**I wish I had a GT**||||reg||1
Z||000002||Shaun41178||12-12-2001||12:35 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by I wish I had a GT:<BR><B>If there is I would be greatly suprised.  There are a lot of variables that would effect the 1/4 time.  Really the best estimation of a time is to double your 1/8 mile.  <P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif"><P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>So let me guess by your statement to get 1/4 mile trap speed you double your 1/8th mile trap speed??  So let me get this straight.  One can run a qtr mile in 18 seconds at a blistering 150 mph??<P>Are you a FU*$^ING retard??  I think you are cause that is the most stupid statement I think I have heard on this forum since this side of Fieroburton.  Come on man, common sense should tell you that you dont' double the time that you ran in the 1/8 to the 1/4.<P>For one you are already going roughly 65-70 mph in a stock fiero v6 at the 1/8 mile.  Which means that you don't have to accelerate to that speed for the last 1/8.  Which means that it won't take you the same amount of time to go the last 1/8 as it does the first.<P>Damn dude!!  Some peoples kids   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>But here is a rough estimate for you 88GTURBO.<P>8.5 second 1/8 will be about a high 12 to a low 13 second qtr mile.<P>usually a 9 second 1/8 will be a high 13 or a low 14 second run.<P>10 second 1/8 will be about a low to mid 15 1/4<P>10.5 will be in the 16's somewhere.<P>This is of course keeping constant acceleration throughout the whole qtr.  Wheelspin and 60' times will affect these times somewhat as well as gearing.<P>My car would run the 1/8 in 8.8-9 seconds flat but would only equal a low 14 - mid 14 run.  Auto tranny puts a damper on top end pull.<P>My God!!!  Think before you say something completely and utterly moronic.  I feel sorry for your kids if you ever are going to have any.<P>------------------<BR>SOLD 85 GT w/ nitrous.<BR>Looking for another.<BR>FOR SALE: Aluminum v6 block.<BR>Shaun41178@hotmail.com<BR>PORN FOREVER!<p>[This message has been edited by Shaun41178 (edited 12-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Nashco||12-12-2001||12:41 AM||||Simma Shaun; I'm sure he'll realize his err, but you don't have to be so harsh dude!<P>As a general "quick idea" most people multiply by 1.55 to get an idea, I've been told.  Of course, this can be way off due to gearing, engine characteristics, etc.  1/4 mile is where you start getting interesting stuff going on between a car that hooks up awesome but doesn't have a great speed and a car that can't hook up, but finishes off like a bat outta hell.  1/8 mile is more generally for quick burst, hook up and go kinda power.  As a side note, a friend of a friend broke into the 5s in the 1/8 the other day....my god that would be wicked!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<BR>*another damn typo*<p>[This message has been edited by Nashco (edited 12-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||DRH||12-12-2001||12:41 AM||||Kinda harsh there, Shaun.||||reg||13
